# 4. Animated SVG Preloader

Create a custom, full-screen preloader for the initial customer website load.

The preloader is an essential brand experience, not a separate page.

## Visual requirements

- Full-screen near-black background.
- Original Brand Store logo centred.
- Animated thin gold circular outline inspired by the logo.
- Gold stroke-drawing effect.
- Subtle logo opacity reveal.
- Elegant brand-name reveal.
- Fine gold progress line or minimal loading indicator.
- Smooth transition into the homepage.

Use the actual uploaded logo. Do not invent a different logo or distort its proportions.

The source logo is a raster image. Preserve it as an image element and create separate SVG decorations around it. Do not claim that the original raster artwork is a fully editable vector SVG.

## Animation sequence

1. Fade in the black background.
2. Draw the gold circular outline using SVG stroke animations.
3. Reveal the logo with a smooth opacity transition.
4. Add a subtle gold shimmer.
5. Reveal the brand name using a fade-in and slight upward movement.
6. Fade the preloader away to reveal the homepage.

Use SVG paths, circles, stroke-dasharray, stroke-dashoffset, opacity, and transforms where appropriate.

Use refined easing curves and avoid spinning the entire logo.

Target a short experience, around 1–2 seconds under normal conditions. Never impose an unnecessary long delay just to show the animation.

## Preloader behaviour

- Show the preloader on the initial application load.
- Do not show it again on every route navigation.
- Prevent an initial white flash.
- Keep the page background consistent with the brand palette.
- Integrate the preloader into the React application lifecycle.
- Handle loading errors gracefully.
- Do not keep the preloader visible indefinitely.
- Clean up timers and event listeners.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Ensure it does not intercept interactions after dismissal.

Create a reusable component such as `BrandPreloader.jsx` and a separate SVG asset or SVG-based component.

